title: Fortios: HA statistics memory
agents: special
catalog: network/fortigate
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors the memory usage of each member of a
 Fortigate HA cluster individually.
 It receives the data from the "monitor/system/ha-statistics" API
 endpoint, which reports statistics per cluster node.
 One service per cluster node is created, named after the hostname
 of the respective node (e.g. "Memory usage cust-fwl-001.domain.local").
 Threshold values are 70% {warn} and 80% {crit} by default.
 The threshold values can be adjusted using the rule
 "FortiOS memory levels".


 The special agent is required for this check,
 which can be configured via “FortiOS”.

item:
 The hostname of the cluster node as reported by the firewall.

discovery:
 One service per cluster node is created.
